@startuml
title Lock / Unlock User Sequence (/api/admin/users/{id}/deactivate or restore)
autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
actor Admin
boundary "Users UI" as UsersPage
control "UsersController\n(FE Dashboard)" as DashboardUsersController
control "AdminUsersController\n(BE API)" as AdminUsersController
control "IAdminUserService" as IAdminUserService
control "AdminUserService" as AdminUserService
entity "User" as UserEntity
entity "Role" as RoleEntity
entity "RefreshToken" as RefreshTokenEntity
control "IAdminUserRepository" as IAdminUserRepository
control "AdminUserRepository" as AdminUserRepository
database "VocaNovaDbContext" as DbContext
database "MySQL Database" as MySQL
note over UsersPage, MySQL
Checked in current code:
Dashboard uses POST /users/{id}/deactivate or /restore.
VocaNovaApiClient calls PATCH /api/admin/users/{id}/deactivate or /restore.
No request DTO body is used; API returns bool in the response envelope.
Entities exist: User, Role and RefreshToken.
Interfaces used in code: IAdminUserService, IAdminUserRepository.
end note
Admin -> UsersPage: Click Lock/Unlock user
UsersPage -> DashboardUsersController: POST /users/{id}/deactivate\nor /users/{id}/restore
DashboardUsersController -> AdminUsersController: VocaNovaApiClient.DeactivateUserAsync(id)\nor RestoreUserAsync(id)
DashboardUsersController -> AdminUsersController: PATCH /api/admin/users/{id}/deactivate\nor /api/admin/users/{id}/restore
AdminUsersController -> AdminUsersController: Check admin authorization
AdminUsersController -> IAdminUserService: DeactivateAsync(id, actorRole)or RestoreAsync(id, actorRole)
IAdminUserService -> AdminUserService: DeactivateAsync(id, actorRole)or RestoreAsync(id, actorRole)
AdminUserService -> IAdminUserRepository: GetStatusTargetAsync(id)
IAdminUserRepository -> AdminUserRepository: GetStatusTargetAsync(id)
AdminUserRepository -> DbContext: Query target user status and role
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT user status and role
MySQL --> DbContext: Target row or null
DbContext -> UserEntity: Materialize User?
DbContext -> RoleEntity: Materialize Role?
UserEntity --> DbContext: User or null
RoleEntity --> DbContext: Role or null
DbContext --> AdminUserRepository: Result
AdminUserRepository --> AdminUserService: Status target or null
alt User not found
AdminUserService --> AdminUsersController: NotFound result
AdminUsersController --> DashboardUsersController: HTTP 404 error
AdminUsersController --> DashboardUsersController: Action failed
DashboardUsersController --> UsersPage: Show feedback
else User cannot be managed
AdminUserService --> AdminUsersController: Forbidden/Conflict result
AdminUsersController --> DashboardUsersController: HTTP 403/409 error
AdminUsersController --> DashboardUsersController: Action failed
DashboardUsersController --> UsersPage: Show feedback
else User can be managed
AdminUserService -> IAdminUserRepository: StageStatusAsync(id, locked/active)
IAdminUserRepository -> AdminUserRepository: StageStatusAsync(id, locked/active)
AdminUserRepository -> UserEntity: Update status
UserEntity --> AdminUserRepository: User updated
AdminUserRepository -> DbContext: Track User status
DbContext -> MySQL: UPDATE users
MySQL --> DbContext: Update result
opt Lock user
AdminUserService -> IAdminUserRepository: RevokeActiveRefreshTokensAsync(id)
IAdminUserRepository -> AdminUserRepository: RevokeActiveRefreshTokensAsync(id)
AdminUserRepository -> RefreshTokenEntity: Set RevokedAt
RefreshTokenEntity --> AdminUserRepository: RefreshToken updated
AdminUserRepository -> DbContext: Track refresh token updates
DbContext -> MySQL: UPDATE refresh_tokens
MySQL --> DbContext: Update result
end
AdminUserService -> IAdminUserRepository: SaveChangesAsync()
IAdminUserRepository -> AdminUserRepository: SaveChangesAsync()
AdminUserRepository -> DbContext: Save changes
DbContext --> AdminUserRepository: Save result
AdminUserRepository --> AdminUserService: Saved
AdminUserService --> AdminUsersController: Success result
AdminUsersController --> DashboardUsersController: HTTP 200 OK
AdminUsersController --> DashboardUsersController: Action success
DashboardUsersController --> UsersPage: Show feedback and refresh page
end
@enduml
